# An alias is the type it names, so aliases that name each other in a ring name no type
# (Semantics ch. 6: `type Name = ...` is "a record, a choice, a newtype, a unit type, an
# alias"). Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
type Alias = Other
type Other = [Alias]

Use: fn Alias -> Nat
fn Use a = 0
